---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy – Month Atlas"
  description="Privacy information for the Month Atlas website and iPhone app."
  lang="en"
  page="privacy"
>
  <article class="legal site-shell py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="text-primary mb-4 text-sm font-bold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">Website and app</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

    <p>This privacy policy explains how personal data is processed when you visit this website or use the Month Atlas iPhone app.</p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <address>
      André Weihe<br />
      c/o Block Services<br />
      Stuttgarter Str. 106<br />
      70736 Fellbach<br />
      Germany<br />
      Email: <a class="link link-primary" href="mailto:andre@andreweihe.de">andre@andreweihe.de</a>
    </address>

    <h2>2. Providing this website</h2>
    <h3>Hosting with GitHub Pages</h3>
    <p>
      This static website is hosted on GitHub Pages. The provider for a free personal GitHub account is GitHub, Inc.,
      88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. GitHub also lists GitHub B.V., Prins Bernhardplein 200,
      1097 JB Amsterdam, the Netherlands, as a possible controller for its own processing.
    </p>
    <p>
      According to GitHub, visiting a GitHub Pages website causes the visitor’s IP address to be logged and stored for security
      purposes. GitHub’s general privacy statement also describes the processing of technical information such as browser,
      operating system, device and request information, date, time and referrer.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest is the secure, reliable and efficient provision of this
      information service. GitHub does not publish a fixed retention period for GitHub Pages access logs. It states that data
      is retained as long as necessary for its purposes and to meet legal obligations, maintain security and enforce agreements.
    </p>
    <p>
      Processing may take place in the USA and other countries. For transfers from the European Economic Area, GitHub refers
      to the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses and states that GitHub, Inc. is certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.
    </p>
    <p>
      For more information, see{" "}
      <a class="link link-primary" href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>
      {" "}and its{" "}
      <a class="link link-primary" href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages">information about GitHub Pages</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>No tracking services of our own</h3>
    <p>
      This website does not embed its own audience analytics, advertising, external fonts, videos or social media content.
      It does not set cookies or use a contact form. Any cookies or similar technologies used by GitHub for its own services
      are governed by GitHub’s terms.
    </p>
    <h3>Language selection in your browser</h3>
    <p>
      On your first visit to the German homepage, your preferred browser language is evaluated locally: German leads to the
      German version; any other language leads to English. Direct links to subpages retain their language. Your language choice
      is stored only in the current browser tab’s sessionStorage, not in cookies or persistent localStorage. It is not sent to an
      analytics service. If session storage is blocked, a manual choice may appear as a lang parameter in the URL.
      The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, for providing the desired language.
    </p>

    <h3>Encryption</h3>
    <p>GitHub Pages serves this website over HTTPS, encrypting the connection between your browser and the website.</p>

    <h2>3. Using the Month Atlas app</h2>
    <h3>Calendar access through EventKit</h3>
    <p>
      Month Atlas requires the full calendar event access provided by iOS to display, create, change and delete calendars’ events.
      The app processes information including calendar names and colors, event titles, times, locations, notes, URLs, recurrence and alerts.
    </p>
    <p>
      Calendar data is managed through Apple’s EventKit and processed in the app for display, search and editing. Month Atlas does
      not operate its own calendar server and does not send calendar names, event content, or event and calendar identifiers to Aptabase.
      If calendar accounts are set up on your iPhone, iOS may synchronize data under the respective calendar provider’s terms.
      Month Atlas has no influence over this.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR, to provide the app functions you request. You can change or revoke calendar access
      in the iOS settings at any time. Without calendar access, the app cannot perform its essential functions.
    </p>

    <h3>Local settings</h3>
    <p>
      The app stores settings on your device for calendar selection, appearance, day panel size, holiday calendar selection,
      app language, event notifications and, where applicable, app-specific calendar colors. It uses the iOS UserDefaults interface
      for this. These settings can be removed by deleting the app. Event content is not stored in a separate app database.
    </p>

    <h3>Local event notifications</h3>
    <p>
      With your iOS notification permission, Month Atlas schedules local notifications for time-based event alerts. Event titles,
      start times, notification times and the identifiers needed to associate notifications with events are passed to the local
      iOS notification system. Scheduled notifications remain stored there until delivery or removal, even when the app is not
      running. There is no app-operated push server; this information is not sent to Aptabase.
    </p>
    <p>
      Event titles and start times may appear on the lock screen. You control their visibility in the iOS notification preview
      settings. You can switch off the app’s event notifications in the app or revoke notification permission in iOS.
      The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR, to provide this function.
    </p>

    <h3>Data-minimizing usage analytics with Aptabase</h3>
    <p>
      Release versions running on physical devices use Aptabase, a service provided by Technov Solutions SRL, Bucharest, Romania.
      The app sends events for app launches, successful event creation, actual changes to a calendar’s color and changes to
      adaptive week height. For week height, the numeric on/off state is also transmitted.
    </p>
    <p>
      Aptabase adds technical information including a timestamp, random session identifier, app and build version, SDK version,
      operating system and version, device model, language and debug status. Country and region are derived from the IP address
      on the server. According to Aptabase, IP addresses and user agents are processed only temporarily in memory and are not
      stored in the analytics dataset. An app-specific daily hash is created using a regularly changing salt;
      the salt is deleted within 48 hours.
    </p>
    <p>
      In particular, Aptabase receives no calendar names, event text, locations, notes, URLs, identifiers or color codes.
      The integration does not use an advertising ID, device ID, cookies or persistent user identifier and is not used to track
      people across apps or websites. Error and crash reporting is not enabled.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest is understanding the actual use of basic functions and
      improving the app accordingly. Aptabase processes data on our behalf in its EU region. For that region, Aptabase lists
      Tinybird Data S.L. in Spain and Amazon Web Services EMEA SARL as subprocessors. According to the provider, analytics data
      is stored for no more than five years, or until the app project in Aptabase or the Aptabase customer account is deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      For more information, see{" "}
      <a class="link link-primary" href="https://aptabase.com/legal/privacy">Aptabase’s privacy policy</a>, its{" "}
      <a class="link link-primary" href="https://aptabase.com/legal/dpa">data processing agreement</a>{" "}and its{" "}
      <a class="link link-primary" href="https://aptabase.com/docs/apple-app-privacy">Apple app privacy guidance</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Contact by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us by email, we process your email address, message and any other information you provide to answer your
      request. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR for contractual or pre-contractual matters; otherwise, it is Article 6(1)(f)
      GDPR, reflecting our legitimate interest in answering enquiries. Data is deleted once the request has been resolved,
      unless statutory retention obligations apply.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Unless this policy specifies a more precise period, we retain personal data only for as long as necessary for the relevant
      purpose or required by law. Following a justified deletion request, data is deleted unless legal grounds require further storage.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Subject to the applicable legal requirements, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the personal data processed about you;</li>
      <li>rectify inaccurate data;</li>
      <li>request erasure or restriction of processing;</li>
      <li>data portability, where the requirements are met;</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests; and</li>
      <li>lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If processing is based on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, you may object on grounds relating to your particular situation.
      To exercise your rights, email{" "}
      <a class="link link-primary" href="mailto:andre@andreweihe.de">andre@andreweihe.de</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Last updated</h2>
    <p>Last updated: November 13, 2026</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
